        <headline>SYSTEMS BLEED AND PRESSURISATION REVIEW</headline>
        <description>BACKGROUND: A REVIEW OF ACMS HAS FOUND LH BLEED PRESSURE TO STILL BE LOW IN CLIMB, AND JUST ABOVE LIMITS IN CRUISE.
THE FOLLOWING COMPONENTS HAVE BEEN REPLACED ON THE LH SIDE SYSTEM OF THIS AIRCRAFT IN THE PAST MONTH:
BAR
PCCV
PRSOV
SENSE LINE 332A2326-45
SENSE LINE 16135-83
SENSE LINE 332A2350-7

ACTION:

1). OBSERVING ALL SAFETY PRECAUTIONS, GAIN ACCESS TO THE AIRCRAFT.

2). LEAK CHECK ALL HSR / HSV / PCCV / BAR SENSE LINES USING SUITABLE LEAK CHECK SPRAY. PAY PARTICULAR ATTENTION TO THE FOLLOWING SENSE LINES:
A) SENSE LINES BETWEEN THE BAR AND PCCV
B) PRSOV SUPPLY PRESSURE SENSE LINE
C) PRSOV DOWNSTREAM PRESSURE SENSE LINE
D) 360 SENSOR SENSE LINES FROM PCCV UNION
E) SENSE LINE TO 450 SENSOR

3). CHECK INSTALLATION OF PRECOOLER SENSE LINE 332A2350-14  WITH REFERENCE TO AMM TASK 36-12-02-400-801 PRECOOLER CONTROL VALVE INSTALLATION.

NOTE: ADJUST THE PRESSURE SENSE LINES TO MAKE SURE THAT THERE IS NO PRELOAD ON THE LINES, OR UNION FITTINGS. PRELOAD CAN CAUSE DAMAGE TO THE LINES.

4). IF NFF, REPLACE THE #1 HSR IAW AMM 36-11-07/401 AND #1 450 SENSOR IAW AMM 36-11-05/401.

5). RETURN THE AIRCRAFT TO SERVICEABLE CONDITION.

**AIRCRAFT IS EQUIPPED WITH ACMS - NO BLEED SHEETS WILL BE REQUIRED.    
**PLEASE ENSURE THAT ALL ELECTRICAL (WHERE APPLICABLE) AND PNEUMATIC FITTINGS / COMPONENTS DISTURBED DURING ABOVE WORKS ARE RE-INSTATED TO CORRECT CONFIGURATION AFTER WORKS.</description>
